            <ArticleTitle>Pain referred to teeth as the sole discomfort in undiagnosed mediastinal lymphoma: report of case.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>587-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The role of routine medical examination in dental diagnosis is described in a report of case involving a young, seemingly healthy patient whose only symptom, pain in the mandibular left molars, proved a manifestation of a malignant mediastinal lymphoma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
